{"name":"Devil Blue","hex":"#277594","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"devil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The chief devil; Satan."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evil creature, the objectification of a hostile and destructive force.","A man with red or orange skin and a pair of horns on his head, a pointed goatee, and a long tail, who carries a pitchfork, represents evil, and is portrayed to children as a boogeyman who punishes bad behavior."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tony Marino","blocks":[{"text":"Tony Silipini was an American professional wrestler better known by his ring name Tony Marino."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/Tony_Marino_resize.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_Marino"},{"title":"Devil","blocks":[{"text":"The devil is a mythical personification of evil as conceived in various cultures and religious traditions. It is seen as the objectification of a hostile and destructive force. Jeffrey Burton Russell states that the different conceptions of the Devil can be summed up as 1. a principle of evil independent from God, 2. an aspect of God, 3. a created being turning evil or 4. a symbol of human evil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/022_devil_representation.JPG/330px-022_devil_representation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/120px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/250px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/120px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Excerpt of a Byzantine-Mosaic-Image. A blue angel, probably representing the Devil, standing before goats. Early 6th century.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlueAngel.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg/500px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm